  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (up to 64 indoor units, Samsung NASA)",
  "applies_to": "Samsung NASA VRF systems: indoor units, AHU, ERV, hot-water and chiller units, up to 64 per gateway.",
  "summary": "Intesis 700 Series multi-protocol gateway set up for BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP on a Samsung NASA bus. It publishes outdoor-unit alarms, gateway-wide commands and one block of objects per indoor unit at (IU x 100): on/off, mode, setpoint, fan, swing, room and discharge temperatures, error code, filter, remote restriction, ventilation, hot water, WindFree, 360 cassette airflow and energy consumption. This file shows the standard indoor unit (IU) set.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Indoor unit instance = (IU x 100) + offset, IU 1-64; IU 1 is shown (100-117).",
    "Left out because they reuse instances of the IU set for other unit types: mode objects for HE, EHS/ERV+ and chiller units, AHU discharge setpoints, hot-water mode and setpoints, water temperatures and the slave-chiller error objects (see the manual).",
    "The outdoor communication-error object is printed with instance OU[0..15] + 1; outdoor unit 00 is shown at BI 1. As printed, OU 15 would land on BI 16, the OU Addressing Error object.",
    "OXXUXX_Air Clean_C (Binary Output) is printed without an instance offset and is left out; OXXUXX_Air Clean_S is BI 107.",
    "Mode numbering here is 1=Heat, 2=Cool, 3=Fan, 4=Dry, 5=Auto, unlike the older INBACSAM manual. Consumption is Wh or kWh as set in MAPS.",
    "The BACnet table has no read/write column; access is inferred from object type. Replaces the INBACSAM004O000-064O000 BACnet servers (listed separately)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "700 Series Air Gateway IN770AIR***O000 - Samsung NASA VRF Systems to Modbus, KNX, BACnet, MQTT and Home Automation - User Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "2025-12-09 v1.0.19",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-in770samxxxo000.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Connect the Samsung NASA R1/R2 bus to AC-Port B (B1 R1, B2 R2), set the outdoor and indoor units to manual addressing, pick BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP in Intesis MAPS, scan the units, send the project, then map each indoor unit's objects from its (IU x 100) block. Check the Unit type object first: other unit types use different objects in the same block.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 100",
        "name": "OXXUXX_On/Off_C",
        "why": "Start/stop indoor unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 100",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Mode IU/AHU_C",
        "why": "Mode command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 100",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Setpoint_C",
        "why": "Setpoint command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 101",
        "name": "OXXUXX_FanSpeed_C",
        "why": "Fan speed command (4 = auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 100",
        "name": "OXXUXX_On/Off_S",
        "why": "Run status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 100",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Setpoint_S",
        "why": "Setpoint in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 101",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Room_Temperature",
        "why": "Indoor unit room temperature, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 102",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Communication Status",
        "why": "Link flags; Exist = unit found on the NASA bus"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 105",
        "name": "OXXUXX_Unit Error code",
        "why": "Fault code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No enable point is documented. OXXUXX_RC Restriction_C (BO 103) restricts the unit's remote controller.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet IP: DHCP for 30 seconds at first start-up, then the default IP 192.168.100.246.",
      "BACnet MS/TP uses the gateway's EIA-485 port.",
      "Units are found and configured in Intesis MAPS; send the project to the gateway after changes."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Global objects (BO 0-3, MO 0-1, AO 0) act on all units at once.",
      "Samsung EHS units need an external sensor for setpoint and room temperature objects.",
      "Manual addressing may be needed on the outdoor units if BI 16 OU Addressing Error is active."
    ]
  },
